{
  "answer": "Candidates C05, C10, and C01 have built retrieval-augmented generation systems using embeddings and vector stores. C05 built a tool using Gemini embeddings stored in PostgreSQL with pgvector (C05#3). C10 led a team building a retrieval-augmented assistant embedded with Gemini and searched with PostgreSQL and pgvector (C10#1). C01 led the build of a support assistant featuring OpenAI and Gemini embeddings and hybrid search on PostgreSQL with pgvector (C01#1).",
  "citations": [
    {
      "ref": "C05#3",
      "quote": "Built a retrieval-augmented question-answering tool over 4,000 pages of equipment manuals: section-aware chunking, Gemini embeddings stored in PostgreSQL with pgvector, and answers that cite page numbers."
    },
    {
      "ref": "C10#1",
      "quote": "Led a team of four building a retrieval-augmented trip assistant: hotel and policy documents chunked by section, embedded with Gemini, and searched with hybrid vector and keyword search in PostgreSQL with pgvector."
    },
    {
      "ref": "C01#1",
      "quote": "Led the build of a retrieval-augmented support assistant that answers questions over 1.2 million account documents; designed the chunking, OpenAI and Gemini embeddings, and hybrid search on PostgreSQL with pgvector."
    }
  ],
  "insufficientEvidence": false
}

